1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
I'm glad you were all able to attend.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Without further ado, I'd like to commence with the Royal Knight Selection Test.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
The exam to decide which knights would fight the Eye of the Midnight Sun had just gotten underway.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
When suddenly, a mysterious man appeared on the scene.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
So sorry I'm late for the party, everybody!

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Who, me? I'm Xerx Lugner. Pleasure's mine.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Despite Asta's immediate distrust of this Xerx, the two of them soon discovered that they had been placed on the same team for the tournament.

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
And so, in this tense and menacing atmosphere, the Royal Knight Selection Test begins in earnest.

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Magic Knights, it's time to start the exam.

13
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Now that the explanations are done, I hope our first two teams are ready.

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
I was born ready, Your Majesty!

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Hm.

16
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Come on!

17
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Thanks, Bobby!

18
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:22,000
38

19
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,920
Oh

20
00:02:52,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Asta! Give those guys a beat and they won't forget!

21
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
That's right! Show them what the Black Bulls are all about!

22
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Give it your best, okay?

23
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Hurry up and take care of them so you can spar with me later!

24
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Don't be reckless!

25
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,000
I swear I'll take my eyes open for the entire battle online at Blake.

26
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Ah! What kind of interesting spells will I get to see today?

27
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
I can't wait to find out!

28
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Here! Anything's more exciting to watch with us!

29
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Why, thank you!

30
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
I'm totally psyched now! It's time to do this thing!

31
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Quit shouting already. This is an exam.

32
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
You need to stay calm and focus.

33
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Look, the best tactic is to study the terrain and figure out what each of us can offer.

34
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
You're right! I hate it, but you're so right!

35
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Everything I say is right, Shortstack, so get used to it.

36
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Settle down now, both of you!

37
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Aw, Asta's cute even when he's gritting his teeth!

38
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:11,000
I agree with Zerks, though. Let's get familiar with each other's abilities and come up with a solid plan.

39
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
I'm sure that's what the other team is doing right now.

40
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Yeah! That's good thinking!

41
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
My plant magic is best suited for support and recovery.

42
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:24,000
And Asta's anti-magic will be useful at close range to nullify the spells our opponents cast.

43
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
What kind of magic do you have, Zerks?

44
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:31,000
What the...?

45
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:37,000
They're already attacking? So fast! And which direction did it come from?

46
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Either way, I've gotta keep our crystal safe!

47
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Oh no! That looked like a long-distance strike. But how was it so accurate?

48
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,000
I don't understand this. Where's it coming from?

49
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Looks like 10 o'clock, 3 meters. Do you copy?

50
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Roger!

51
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Thanks to a highly precise crystal magic spell called Crystal Scope, their whereabouts are as clear as, well... you know.

52
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
I'll make you pay for ridiculing the Wizard King, knave!

53
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
You don't deserve a chance to shine after that stunt!

54
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Claim magic, burst javelin!

55
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Combined with rock magic, Strongbow!

56
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:23,000
We're gonna lose!

57
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Craft, what now? We work together, we...

58
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Seriously, what is the matter with this guy?!

59
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,000
He's terrible!

60
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,000
He's... asleep?

61
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Yep, he's out cold.

62
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Sure looks like it.

63
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Guess he needs a nap.

64
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,000
That's pathetic.

65
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
How could anybody fall asleep with all these people watching him?!

66
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,000
The shame! The embarrassment!

67
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:55,000
My, I never expected a tournament like this to devolve into nap time. They must be worn out. Unless... it's a trick.

68
00:05:55,000 --> 00:06:02,000
What the heck are you laying on the ground for, huh?! If you don't get off your lazy butt right now, our team's crystal is gonna be smashed to pieces!

69
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Do you wanna win this thing or not?! You're such a jerk!

70
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Winning or losing doesn't make a difference to me.

71
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Nor do I care how badly you wanna win. So just direct all that unchecked enthusiasm elsewhere.

72
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Listen, I kinda pulled an all-nighter last night. I'd appreciate it if you two would let me catch a few Z's.

73
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:25,000
That Zerk's fellow actually has the nerve to sleep.

74
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
Do you think it's some kind of strategy?

75
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:33,000
It's not. My crystal scope can identify not just location, but the physical state of its targets.

76
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:36,000
There's no doubt that Ruffian is fast asleep.

77
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:42,000
How can one man be so arrogant, especially after the way he insulted the Wizard King when he first arrived?

78
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,000
